  "exemptions": {
    "files": [
      {
        "path": "app.go",
        "kind": "facade-surface",
        "reason": "ADR-010 Wails facade: 116 methods, each a one-line delegate to presentation.AppAPI, with no branching of its own. Wails binds a single struct, so splitting the file would scatter one binding surface across several files without removing a single decision from it. It grows with the API, not with complexity."
      }
    ],
    "functions": [
      {
        "symbol": "internal/infra/plugin/ipc/host_server.go::HostServer.HandleRequest",
        "kind": "dispatch-table",
        "reason": "One flat switch over the plugin RPC method names, three or four lines per arm, every arm delegating to a capability proxy. The length is the size of the protocol surface, not of a decision. Splitting it into per-method handlers would scatter the one place where the capability gate, the method name and the proxy it reaches are visible together, which is exactly what a reviewer needs to read in one screen."
      }
    ]
  },
